<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konrad I of Głogów</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1228–<a href="/years/1274">1274</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konrad I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glogow">Głogów</a> was a Silesian Piast duke, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-the-pious">Henry II the Pious</a>, who was killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a> in 1241. First intended for the church, he received Głogów in a division of the family lands around 1251 and founded a separate duchy there. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-glogow">Henry III of Głogów</a> became one of the most powerful Silesian princes.</p></div>
